			<div class="content" id="post-content-4147478">
									

<p>Minimal skips are tricky pull off, especially when they rely on fairly intricate concepts like this one. When done poorly, they tend to feel like they should be labeled &quot;Some Assembly Required&quot;; without a demonstration of the concept, the reader's imagination has to do the bulk of the heavy lifting to make the article interesting.</p>
<p>When done well, as I think you've done, the base concept feels like a fully-formed playground for the reader's imagination to romp in. You also have a concept that invites the reader to project their own experiences and feelings onto it, which dovetails perfectly into the themes at play, which is quite elegant.</p>

							</div>

								
					
